#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *First vs Second Backward Classes Commission:* *Kaka Kalelkar* chaired the 1st (1953); *B.P. Mandal* chaired the 2nd (1978). Never confuse them!
  2. *Mandal Quota vs Population:* Mandal identified OBCs as *52%* of population, but recommended a *27% quota* to stay within the 50% legal limit.
  3. *Creamy Layer Mandate:* The Supreme Court in *Indra Sawhney (1992)* did NOT strike down OBC quotas; it *upheld* them with creamy layer exclusion.
  4. *1989 Outside Supporters:* V.P. Singh was supported by *both the BJP and the Left Front*, neither of which joined the government.
  5. *First Non-Congress 5-Year Term:* The *NDA government (1999–2004)* completed 5 years; the 1977 Janata Party government collapsed after 2.5 years.
  6. *Gujral Doctrine Essence:* Based on *non-reciprocity* (unilateral goodwill to smaller neighbours), NOT on strict mutual quid-pro-quo.
  7. *Single-Party Majority Year:* 2014 was the first single-party majority (BJP 282) *since 1984*, ending 30 years of hung parliaments.
]

