= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Fifteen authentic CUET UG examination-standard multiple-choice questions testing conceptual, chronological, institutional, and factual mastery. Marking scheme: $+5$ for correct answer, $-1$ for incorrect attempt.

== Part 1: The 1989 Transition, National Front & Mandal Commission

#mcq(1, [Which year marked the formal end of the single-party 'Congress System' at the Centre, inaugurating a quarter-century of coalition governments?], (
  [1977], [1984], [1989], [1996],
))

#solution(1, [The 1989 general election ended single-party Congress dominance at the Centre; although Congress won 197 seats, it chose to sit in opposition, ushering in multi-party coalition rule.], answer: [C])

#mcq(2, [The National Front government led by Prime Minister V.P. Singh in 1989 was supported from the outside by which unique ideological pairing?], (
  [Congress and CPI], [The Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and the Left Front], [AIADMK and DMK], [Janata Party and Swatantra Party],
))

#solution(2, [The National Front government under V.P. Singh was supported from the outside simultaneously by both the right-wing BJP and the Left Front, sitting on opposite sides of the house.], answer: [B])

#mcq(3, [Under Article 340 of the Indian Constitution, who chaired the Second Backward Classes Commission appointed by the Morarji Desai government in 1978?], (
  [Bindeshwari Prasad Mandal (B.P. Mandal)], [Kaka Kalelkar], [Jagjivan Ram], [Chaudhary Charan Singh],
))

#solution(3, [The Second Backward Classes Commission was appointed in December 1978 under the chairmanship of B.P. Mandal. Kaka Kalelkar chaired the First Commission in 1953.], answer: [A])

#mcq(4, [In which landmark verdict did a nine-judge Constitution bench of the Supreme Court uphold the 27% OBC reservation while capping total reservations at 50% and excluding the 'creamy layer'?], (
  [Kesavananda Bharati Case (1973)], [Minerva Mills Case (1980)], [Indra Sawhney v. Union of India (1992)], [S.R. Bommai Case (1994)],
))

#solution(4, [In Indra Sawhney v. Union of India (1992), a 9-judge bench validated the 27% OBC quota, imposed a 50% ceiling on total reservations, and mandated the exclusion of the creamy layer.], answer: [C])

#mcq(5, [The 'Gujral Doctrine', formulating five principles of non-reciprocal unilateral goodwill towards India's South Asian neighbours, was propounded by Prime Minister:], (
  [I.K. Gujral], [P.V. Narasimha Rao], [H.D. Deve Gowda], [Atal Bihari Vajpayee],
))

#solution(5, [Inder Kumar Gujral authored the Gujral Doctrine, advocating unilateral, non-reciprocal goodwill and concessions by India towards smaller South Asian neighbors.], answer: [A])

#pagebreak()
== Part 2: Coalition Tenures, Rights Acts & Bahujan Resurgence

#mcq(6, [Which was the first non-Congress coalition government in post-independence India to complete a full five-year term in office?], (
  [The Janata Party Government (1977–1982)], [The National Democratic Alliance (NDA) led by Atal Bihari Vajpayee from 1999 to 2004], [The United Front Government (1996–2001)], [The United Progressive Alliance (2004–2009)],
))

#solution(6, [The NDA government under Atal Bihari Vajpayee, elected in October 1999 following the Kargil War, governed until May 2004, completing the first non-Congress full five-year term.], answer: [B])

#mcq(7, [According to political scientist Yogendra Yadav's analytical framework, the 'Second Democratic Upsurge' in Indian politics was primarily marked by:], (
  [The introduction of universal adult suffrage in the 1950s], [The youth-driven aspirational voting and digitisation post-2014], [The adoption of Liberalisation, Privatisation, and Globalisation in 1991], [The electoral mobilisation and political empowerment of Other Backward Classes (OBCs) and Dalits],
))

#solution(7, [Yogendra Yadav identified the Second Democratic Upsurge (1980s–1990s) as the social justice and Mandal mobilisation of Other Backward Classes and Dalits entering state power.], answer: [D])

#mcq(8, [Which landmark rights-based act guaranteeing 100 days of guaranteed wage employment to rural households was enacted by the UPA-I government in 2005?], (
  [Right to Information Act], [Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA)], [Right to Education Act], [National Food Security Act],
))

#solution(8, [The Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) was enacted in 2005 under UPA-I, providing a statutory guarantee of 100 days of rural wage employment.], answer: [B])

#mcq(9, [The minority government led by Prime Minister Chandra Shekhar in 1990–1991 came to power with the outside floor support of which party?], (
  [Bharatiya Janata Party], [Left Front], [Indian National Congress led by Rajiv Gandhi], [Telugu Desam Party],
))

#solution(9, [Following the collapse of the V.P. Singh ministry in November 1990, Chandra Shekhar formed the Samajwadi Janata Party, governing with outside support from Rajiv Gandhi's Congress.], answer: [C])

#mcq(10, [In the 2014 general election, how many seats did the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) secure on its own, winning the first single-party parliamentary majority in 30 years?], (
  [282 seats], [272 seats], [303 seats], [336 seats],
))

#solution(10, [In the 2014 Lok Sabha elections, the BJP won 282 seats on its own (while the NDA won 336 seats), crossing the 272-seat majority mark for the first single-party majority since 1984.], answer: [A])

