== Part 3: Subaltern Mobilisation, Electoral Crises & Political Consensus

#mcq(11, [The Bahujan Samaj Party (BSP), established in 1984 to represent the interests of Bahujans (SC, ST, OBC, and religious minorities), was founded under the leadership of:], (
  [Dr. B.R. Ambedkar], [Jagjivan Ram], [Mayawati], [Kanshi Ram],
))

#solution(11, [Kanshi Ram founded the Bahujan Samaj Party (BSP) in 1984 to mobilize the Bahujan Samaj (comprising 85% of society) to capture state power and dismantle caste hierarchy.], answer: [D])

#mcq(12, [BAMCEF (Backward and Minority Communities Employees Federation), which served as the organizational precursor to the Dalit political resurgence, was established in 1978 by:], (
  [Kanshi Ram], [Ram Vilas Paswan], [Chaudhary Charan Singh], [Karpoori Thakur],
))

#solution(12, [Kanshi Ram organized educated government servants from marginalized communities into BAMCEF in 1978, establishing an autonomous institutional vanguard for subaltern politics.], answer: [A])

#mcq(13, [In the 1996 General Elections, Atal Bihari Vajpayee was sworn in as Prime Minister for the first time, but resigned after how many days due to lack of majority support?], (
  [10 days], [13 days], [30 days], [60 days],
))

#solution(13, [Atal Bihari Vajpayee was sworn in as Prime Minister in May 1996 as leader of the single largest party, but resigned after 13 days unable to secure coalition partners.], answer: [B])

#mcq(14, [The First Backward Classes Commission in post-independence India was appointed in 1953 under the chairmanship of:], (
  [B.P. Mandal], [Justice J.C. Shah], [Kaka Kalelkar], [Justice G.T. Nanavati],
))

#solution(14, [The First Backward Classes Commission was appointed under Article 340 in 1953 under the chairmanship of Kaka Kalelkar, submitting its report in 1955.], answer: [C])

#mcq(15, [In the coalition era post-1989, what became the standard institutional mechanism for managing ideological differences and guiding policy decisions among coalition partners?], (
  [Issuing presidential ordinances], [Enforcing a single party constitution on all partners], [Amending the Tenth Schedule anti-defection law], [The drafting and adoption of a Common Minimum Programme (CMP)],
))

#solution(15, [Coalitions such as the United Front, NDA, and UPA routinely navigated disparate ideological platforms by drafting and adhering to a formal Common Minimum Programme (CMP).], answer: [D])

